t that was by far the scariest  we had things really moving we were  you know again economy was roaring we  had great people in place we had plans  we were building for second term and  then covet comes out of nowhere and and  really  hit the world like a ton of bricks and  you know i write about in the book my  experience getting pulled in again not  as a medical expert but just as somebody  to help operationally who knew how to  move the levers of government vice  president pence who i worked very  closely with asked me to come on and  help him  um you know execute with certain things  like scale testing and whatnot  but it was very interesting so you're  making a lot of uh decisions uh the  media was the first thing they got trump  on right because if he was more careful  than he was killing jobs if he was  opening the economy he was killing  people and so cnn kept those tickers up  you know depending on the day and and  they were loving the fact that they can  just bludgeon him you could always find  a nurse who's afraid they're going to  run out of stuff and we were playing  racquetball i mean i had stories you  know that i write about where  i'd see a nurse on cnn complaining they  don't have masks at a hospital i get on  the phone with the head of the hospital  and say what do you need okay we'll get  it to you and we we made sure all these  shortages that everyone was fearing  were going to happen did not happen a  lot of us because we thought like  business people not like bureaucrats  right so i tell stories about how you  know we find all these masks we figure  how to do dpas and to get them in order  to get them over we don't have enough  planes as us so i called fred smith i  called david abney from ups and fedex  and i said look we need your planes and  they're like they're your air force take  them like anything you do and even david  abney told me months later i've never  seen anything like it in my career as  quickly as i could land played in asia  